.TH XPN-CLIENT-SETUP 8 "October 2026" "XPN"
.SH NAME
xpn-client-setup \- install an XPN client service with automatic retries
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo xpn-client-setup
.I profile.json
.RB [ --name " alta" ]
.RB [ --no-start ]
.RB [ --inner-encryption " on|off" ]
.RB [ --require-pq ]
.RB [ --single-stream ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Copies an already enrolled profile into /etc/xpn/clients with mode 0600,
creates and enables a named systemd unit, and starts it unless --no-start is used.
Unchanged reruns do not restart an active service. Requires an updated XPN client
with built-in retry support. No C compilation or account creation is performed.
.PP
The unit runs xpn connect directly. The client retries network failures
indefinitely with equal jitter: 5-10, 10-20, 20-40,
40-80, 80-160, then 150-300 seconds. Backoff resets after a connection lasts
120 seconds. Startup is spread over 0-5 seconds. Manual stop cancels retries.
Certificate checks, authentication and encryption policy are never relaxed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --name NAME
Service suffix, default default. Produces xpn-client-NAME.service.
.TP
.B --no-start
Enable at boot without starting now. Changed active configurations are stopped.
.TP
.B --retry-initial SECONDS
Initial retry ceiling; default 10. Delay is half to all of the ceiling.
.TP
.B --retry-max SECONDS
Maximum retry ceiling; default 300, allowed up to 3600.
.TP
.B --stable-seconds SECONDS
Authenticated uptime required to reset backoff; default 120.
.SH NETWORKING
The launcher restores ordinary networking between attempts and when stopped.
This is not an always-on kill switch. Full-tunnel connections may interrupt SSH.
Use a split-tunnel profile for initial remote testing. Separate services require
separate device profiles; multiple full tunnels can conflict.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/xpn/clients/NAME.json
.br
.I /etc/systemd/system/xpn-client-NAME.service
.br
.I /var/backups/xpn-client/TIMESTAMP/changes.md
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xpn (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
